{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The mountain of Elohim, Horeb.</b> So Moses wrote. The meaning of Horeb: because of the intense heat, since no rain descends there — for it is near Egypt, a three-day journey as Moses spoke — and because the Nile is distant, therefore there is no moisture there, and dryness prevails in it."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:08.460416636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}